@baseUrl = http://localhost:5205
@contentType = application/json

### CASE 01 - Valid Competitor, partly paid (201)
# @name createCompetitor
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1001",
  "registrationType": "Competitor",
  "amountPaid": 1000.00
}

### CASE 02 - Valid Exhibitor, unpaid (201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{"participantName":"Maria Santos","contactNumber":"09181234567","email":"maria@example.com","address":"Sorsogon City","carMakeModel":"Honda Civic Type R","plateNumber":"TST 1002","registrationType":"Exhibitor","amountPaid":0}

### CASE 03 - Valid VIP, fully paid (201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{"participantName":"Pedro Reyes","contactNumber":"09191234567","email":"pedro@example.com","address":"Naga City","carMakeModel":"Nissan Skyline R34","plateNumber":"TST 1003","registrationType":"VIP","amountPaid":5000}

### CASE 04 - Registration numbers increase: compare cases 01-03
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations?page=1&pageSize=10

### CASE 05 - Client-supplied server fields are ignored
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{"participantName":"Test User","contactNumber":"09171234567","email":"test@example.com","address":"Test Address","carMakeModel":"Toyota 86","plateNumber":"TST 1005","registrationType":"VIP","amountPaid":0,"registrationFee":1,"status":"Confirmed","registrationNumber":"HACK-1"}

### CASE 06 - All required text fields empty (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{"participantName":"","contactNumber":"","email":"","address":"","carMakeModel":"","plateNumber":"","registrationType":"Competitor","amountPaid":0}

### CASE 07 - Invalid contact number (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{"participantName":"Test","contactNumber":"12345","email":"test@example.com","address":"Address","carMakeModel":"Toyota","plateNumber":"TST 1007","registrationType":"Competitor","amountPaid":0}

### CASE 08 - Invalid email (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{"participantName":"Test","contactNumber":"09171234567","email":"not-an-email","address":"Address","carMakeModel":"Toyota","plateNumber":"TST 1008","registrationType":"Competitor","amountPaid":0}

### CASE 09 - Amount paid is negative (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{"participantName":"Test","contactNumber":"09171234567","email":"test@example.com","address":"Address","carMakeModel":"Toyota","plateNumber":"TST 1009","registrationType":"Competitor","amountPaid":-1}

### CASE 10 - Amount paid exceeds fee (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{"participantName":"Test","contactNumber":"09171234567","email":"test@example.com","address":"Address","carMakeModel":"Toyota","plateNumber":"TST 1010","registrationType":"Competitor","amountPaid":2501}

### CASE 11 - Invalid registration type (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{"participantName":"Test","contactNumber":"09171234567","email":"test@example.com","address":"Address","carMakeModel":"Toyota","plateNumber":"TST 1011","registrationType":"Sponsor","amountPaid":0}

### CASE 12 - Participant name longer than 150 characters (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{"participantName":"xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx","contactNumber":"09171234567","email":"test@example.com","address":"Address","carMakeModel":"Toyota","plateNumber":"TST 1012","registrationType":"Competitor","amountPaid":0}

### CASE 13 - Duplicate plate (use TST 1001 from case 01; 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{"participantName":"Duplicate","contactNumber":"09171234567","email":"dup@example.com","address":"Address","carMakeModel":"Toyota","plateNumber":"TST 1001","registrationType":"VIP","amountPaid":0}

### CASE 14 - Default list, page 1 pageSize 10
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations

### CASE 15 - Newest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations?page=1&pageSize=10

### CASE 16 - Second page, custom size
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations?page=2&pageSize=5

### CASE 17 - Page past the end
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations?page=999

### CASE 18 - Invalid page (400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations?page=0

### CASE 19 - Page size too large (400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations?pageSize=100

### CASE 20 - Filter by type
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations?type=VIP

### CASE 21 - Filter by status
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations?status=Confirmed

### CASE 22 - Search participant name
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations?participantName=juan

### CASE 23 - Search ignores case
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations?participantName=JUAN

### CASE 24 - Partial name match
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations?participantName=dela

### CASE 25 - Combined filters
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations?type=Competitor&status=Pending&participantName=juan

### CASE 26 - No matches
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations?participantName=zzzzzz

### CASE 27 - Invalid type (400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations?type=Sponsor

### CASE 28 - Invalid status (400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations?status=Done

### CASE 29 - Existing ID (replace GUID with an ID from list/create response)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

### CASE 30 - ID that does not exist (404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000099

### CASE 31 - Invalid GUID route does not crash (404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations/abc

### CASE 32 - Summary returns all KPI fields
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations/summary

### CASE 33 - Status counts add up; compare summary counts
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations/summary

### CASE 34 - Summary totalRegistrations matches list totalCount
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations?page=1&pageSize=10

### CASE 35 - Money totals: totalFees - totalPayments = uncollectedPayments
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations/summary

### CASE 36 - Cancelled registrations excluded from money totals
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations/summary

### CASE 37 - Summary updates after new registration (then re-run summary)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{"participantName":"Summary Check","contactNumber":"09171234567","email":"summary@example.com","address":"Sorsogon","carMakeModel":"Toyota 86","plateNumber":"TST 1037","registrationType":"Exhibitor","amountPaid":500}

### CASE 38 - Summary route is not treated as an ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations/summary

### CASE 39 - SQLite persistence: restart API then re-run list and a known ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations

### CASE 40 - Unique indexes: inspect Registrations indexes in DB Browser for SQLite
# Manual database inspection: IX_Registrations_PlateNumber and IX_Registrations_RegistrationNumber must both be unique.
